{
  "id": "my-green-garden",
  "title": "My Green Garden",
  "level": "A1",
  "summary": "What do plants need to grow? Come and see my garden!",
  "teachingMethod": "CLIL",
  "teachingMethodReason": "Meets Coyle, Hood & Marsh (2010)'s 4 C's Framework at the simplest level the library supports. Content - real biology (plants need water, light and soil to grow), not just garden vocabulary. Communication - \"need + noun\" and the simple present for general truths are the vehicle for that content. Cognition - the reader links a need to an outcome (the plant has all three things, so it grows), which is more than recall. Culture - the closing page notes that people grow plants everywhere in the world. Deliberately kept to three needs with one short sentence each, because zoe-animal-homes showed how quickly a CLIL book at A1 drifts above its level.",
  "grammarFeatures": [
    "Simple present tense for general facts",
    "\"Need + noun\" to say what something must have",
    "\"There are\" for saying what exists",
    "Descriptive adjectives (green, dark, warm)"
  ],
  "introFunFacts": [
    "🌱 This book tells you real science! Plants need three things, and you will learn all of them.",
    "🧃 Watch for the word 'need' - it means you cannot live without that thing.",
    "🔍 At the end, try to remember all three things a plant needs. Ready?"
  ],
